WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.540
Have a heart? Then think about donating it.

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:03.820
Have you signed up?

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:07.500
Go to organ donor.gov and share the gift of life.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.900
I clicked the box.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.160
But most people don’t.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.420
As a result, more than 100,000

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.260
people wait hoping to get a kidney.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:16.840
Most wait years.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.740
one of three waiting on that list will die

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.140
because there is simply not enough organs

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:22.880
available.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.760
whenever demand exceeds supply,

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.740
black markets appear.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.380
Profits are huge.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.840
Single organ selling for up to $200,000.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.540
So why not legalize the sale!?

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.360
Then there would be no need for black markets.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.740
Legalization would make transplants safer

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:41.960
and bring prices down.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.400
People legally sell blood, plasma,

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.600
sperm, eggs, bone marrow.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.580
Why not a kidney?

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:51.400
Poor people are going to be hurt.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.120
philosophy professor Sam Kerstein advised

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.020
the World Health Organization, which supports

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.280
the laws that ban selling organs.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.300
Body parts to be put into Americans will come

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.380
from poor countries.

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:08.580
I don’t want to see poor people in Pakistan

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:11.260
having their lives truncated.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:14.660
Having to go through psychology difficulties.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:17.740
But these people may want to make other choices

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:20.920
and who are we to tell them “you may not”.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:24.920
We are people who care about people who are

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.680
different from us and poorer than we are.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.200
That's why we care.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.400
Deep moralisms about the dignity of human

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.619
life being degraded by commercialism

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:37.860
it's all crap.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.700
Law professor Lloyd Cohen, 24 years ago went

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.200
on 60-Minutes to argue that people should

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.240
be allowed to sell a body part.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.400
Transplant surgeons make money, transplant

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.880
physicians makes money, hospitals make money,

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:51.900
drug companies make money.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:55.800
Everybody can get paid except the person

00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:01.060
who is delivering the irreplaceable part.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.400
In the years since Cohen first argued for

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.000
legal sales, thousands of people on

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.300
the growing wait lists died.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:11.100
Without a financial incentive not enough people

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.560
give up an organ.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.280
financial incentives work for everything!

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.740
They work for food, they work for housing

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.100
they work for clothing.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.760
This is exploiting the weak and the poor.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.660
We heard the same argument with regard to

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.140
things like surrogacy.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.860
Then you interview the women.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:30.640
This is a wonderful thing that they can do

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:32.500
and they can get paid.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.240
[prayer]

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.400
Oddly the one country that allows the selling

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.760
of organs is Iran.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.780
And this PBS report says --

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.520
The market has slashed the waiting time

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.840
for a kidney down to around a year

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.220
When Iran made it legal, there were more kidneys

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:50.380
available and they were cheaper.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:52.980
And a very high percentage of them say they

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.440
regret it. They say that

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.900
their psychological health has decreased.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.700
They say that their physical health has decreased.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.010
They're really suffering.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:03.620
But another study concluded that most donors

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.320
did not regret it.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:08.160
So you've got that on one side of the scale.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:11.500
So you put on the other side of the scale

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.080
vacuous moralisms about our consciousness

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.340
of the human body being

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:19.900
degraded by crass commercialism.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:22.300
And it don't carry much weight.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:26.760
But it does, the vacuous moralisms are winning.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.840
You've been talking about this for years

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:30.239
why hasn't it happened?

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.000
There aren't enough people who want it

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.260
and so it just dies.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:38.180
Then after years of arguing for legalization

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:40.420
Suddenly your kidney stops working.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:44.180
All men are mortal and Cohen is a man.

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:45.620
Now he needs a kidney.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.580
Cohen’s become one of the growing number of

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.780
Americans waiting for one.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:53.940
He’s unlikely get one, and he won’t
turn to the black market.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:55.948
But there's a wonderful group

00:03:55.948 --> 00:03:57.540
called Matching Donors.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:00.560
It connects voluntary donors with people who

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:01.520
need organs.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.140
And you put up your profile about

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.900
what it is you need.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:07.090
It's rather embarrassing.

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:11.360
I am known by my family, friends for my integrity

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:14.220
my humor, and my incredible good looks.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.280
My son said to put that in.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:17.780
And he may have found a donor.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:23.180
At least one very kind sympathetic lady has found

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:26.880
my story relatively compelling.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.560
She is being tested to see if she is

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.000
healthy enough to donate.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.240
If not, Cohen will be back on the waiting list,

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:36.100
with about 100,000 other Americans,

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:40.040
receiving expensive dialysis, week after week.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:43.580
Spending on dialysis alone accounts for nearly

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:45.440
get this, one percent of

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:47.580
the entire federal budget.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.300
Many of those people will die because no one

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:53.780
is allowed to buy or sell a kidney.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:56.740
Organs that could restore people to health

00:04:56.740 --> 00:05:00.920
and extend life are instead being buried and burned.

